    <div class="code-spotlight">
        <div class="code-card">
            <header>
                <span class="file-tag">Python (Pandas)</span>
                <h4>Panel Harmonization</h4>
            </header>
            <div class="code-inner">
                <pre><code># Aligning disparate census rounds into a unified panel
def harmonize_census(df, year):
    df['YEAR'] = year
    # Mapping registration districts to stable units
    df['RD_ID'] = df['REGDIST'].map(rd_lookup_1851)
    return df.set_index(['RD_ID', 'YEAR'])</code></pre>
            </div>
            <footer>
                <p>Crucial for handling changing administrative boundaries between 1851 and 1881.</p>
            </footer>
        </div>

        <div class="code-card">
            <header>
                <span class="file-tag">Econometrics (Statsmodels)</span>
                <h4>The Identification Logic</h4>
            </header>
            <div class="code-inner">
                <pre><code># Difference-in-Differences Estimation
model = sm.PanelOLS.from_formula(
    'TFR ~ treat_intensity * post_act + IMR + C(YEAR) + EntityEffects',
    data=panel_df
)
results = model.fit(cov_type='clustered', cluster_entity=True)</code></pre>
            </div>
            <footer>
                <p>Standard Errors are clustered at the district level to account for spatial and temporal autocorrelation.</p>
            </footer>
        </div>
    </div>

